=== 1. CONTROL: the twelve avx512 rows, declared before the run ===
If these move, the scalar reading is about the host. #147 measured every
avx512 row within 0.97-1.10 of its width-8 median at width 1.
  pass a  w4/w8 ns ratio over 12 avx512 rows: 0.995-1.005
  pass a  w2/w8 ns ratio over 12 avx512 rows: 0.999-1.050
  pass a  w1/w8 ns ratio over 12 avx512 rows: 0.990-1.054
  pass b  w4/w8 ns ratio over 12 avx512 rows: 0.972-1.002
  pass b  w2/w8 ns ratio over 12 avx512 rows: 0.998-1.001
  pass b  w1/w8 ns ratio over 12 avx512 rows: 0.984-1.030
  worst deviation from 1.000: 0.054 at pass a w1

=== 2. DRIFT: pass A (8,4,2,1) against pass B (1,2,4,8) ===
Within-pass ratios to that pass's own w8 arm. A real width effect reads the
same in both passes; a drift monotone in time does not, because the two
passes visit each width at mirrored positions in the clock.
  w4: ratio_A/ratio_B over 20 rows: 0.865-1.150  median 1.000
  w2: ratio_A/ratio_B over 20 rows: 0.867-1.398  median 1.002
  w1: ratio_A/ratio_B over 20 rows: 0.868-1.154  median 1.003
  raw cross-pass agreement at each width (median_A/median_B, same width):
    w8: 0.867-1.153  median 1.000
    w4: 0.868-1.150  median 1.000
    w2: 0.999-1.212  median 1.002
    w1: 0.998-1.071  median 1.002

